      "traceTextDiagram": "Wide Event Creation and Emission Flow\n├── Event Builder Creation\n│   └── NewEvent(operation) \u003c-- 1a\n│       └── initializes WideEvent with timestamp \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/builder.go:42\n│           and span ID\n├── Builder Configuration\n│   ├── WithComponent/WithCommand/WithData \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/builder.go:68\n│   │   └── fluent API methods\n│   └── EnrichFromEnv/EnrichFromContext \u003c-- 1b\n│       └── populates session, agent, workspace \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/builder.go:174\n├── Event Finalization\n│   └── Success/Error/Canceled \u003c-- 1c\n│       └── finalize() sets status \u0026 duration \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/builder.go:240\n│           └── generates trace_id if missing \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/builder.go:243\n└── Event Emission Pipeline\n    ├── Emit(ctx, event) \u003c-- 1d\n    │   ├── getObsDir() check \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/emitter.go:48\n    │   └── getSampler() \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/emitter.go:27\n    │       └── ShouldSample(event) \u003c-- 1e\n    │           ├── returns Drop/Sample/AlwaysSample\n    │           └── if not Drop: \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/emitter.go:57\n    │               └── WriteEvent() \u003c-- 1f\n    │                   └── writes to wide_events.ndjson\n    └── EmitSync() for critical events \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/emitter.go:70\n        └── bypasses sampling",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen debugging distributed systems, you need to understand **what happened to a request**, not just what your code did. Traditional narrow logging (e.g., \"entering function X\", \"variable Y = 5\") generates thousands of lines that obscure the signal. The wide event system solves this by emitting **one comprehensive event per operation** [1a] that captures all context needed for debugging: timing, outcome, business context (session, workspace), and domain-specific metrics.\n\nThe system follows **tail-based sampling** [1e]: always record errors and slow requests (the interesting ones), but only sample 5% of fast, healthy requests. This keeps disk usage manageable while ensuring you never miss a problem.\n\n## Details\n\n### Builder Pattern\n\nEvents are constructed using a fluent builder API [1a]. You create an event with `NewEvent(operation)`, chain configuration methods like `WithComponent()` and `WithWorkspace()`, then finalize with `Success()`, `Error()`, or `Canceled()` [1c]. The builder automatically generates trace IDs and timestamps.\n\n**Enrichment** [1b] pulls business context from environment variables (`FOXCTL_SESSION_ID`, `FOXCTL_AGENT_ID`) and the context object, so you don't have to manually thread this data through your code.\n\n### Emission Pipeline\n\nWhen you call `Emit()` [1d], the event goes through sampling [1e]. The sampler checks: Is this an error? Is it slow (\u003e1s by default)? If not, apply random sampling (5% by default). Only sampled events proceed to disk.\n\n**Persistence** [1f] writes events as NDJSON (newline-delimited JSON) to `$FOXCTL_OBS_DIR/events/wide_events.ndjson`. Each line is a complete JSON object. Files are append-only; external tools (OTEL Collector, logrotate) handle rotation and shipping.\n\n### Configuration\n\nSet `FOXCTL_OBS_DIR` to enable observability. If unset, all emission is a no-op. Sampling behavior is controlled by `FOXCTL_OBS_SAMPLE_ERRORS` (default: true), `FOXCTL_OBS_SLOW_THRESHOLD_MS` (default: 1000), and `FOXCTL_OBS_SAMPLE_RATE` (default: 0.05)."
    },
