          "lineNumber": 69,
          "lineContent": "builder.WithResultArtifact(artifacts.Result)",
          "title": "Artifact Digest Capture",
          "description": "Adds CAS digest to enable full response replay from observability events"
        },
        {
          "id": "2e",
          "path": "internal/runservice/observability.go",
          "lineNumber": 74,
          "lineContent": "done(err)",
          "title": "Span Completion",
          "description": "Finalizes and emits event with success/error/canceled status based on execution result"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Runservice Skill Execution Observability Flow\n│\n├── Executor.ExecuteSync() entry \u003c-- internal/runservice/jobs.go:129\n│   └── jobStore.ExecutePreparedSkill() \u003c-- 2a\n│       └── (skill binary executes)\n│\n├── Executor.emitWideEventWithArtifacts() \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:47\n│   ├── observability.StartSpanAt() \u003c-- 2b\n│   │   ├── WithSpanTraceID(CorrelationID) \u003c-- 2c\n│   │   ├── WithSpanComponent(ComponentSkill) \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:54\n│   │   ├── WithSpanCommand(skill name) \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:55\n│   │   └── WithSpanSubtype(\"runservice\") \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:57\n│   │\n│   ├── builder.WithData(\"correlation_id\") \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:62\n│   ├── builder.WithData(\"source\", source) \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:64\n│   ├── builder.WithData(\"cache_hit\") \u003c-- internal/runservice/observability.go:65\n│   │\n│   ├── builder.WithResultArtifact() \u003c-- 2d\n│   │   └── (CAS digest for replay capability)\n│   │\n│   └── done(err) \u003c-- 2e\n│       └── observability.Emit() \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:202\n│           └── (event written to disk)",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen foxctl executes skills, operators need visibility into **what happened during each execution** for debugging, performance analysis, and audit trails. The challenge is capturing comprehensive context—correlation IDs, execution source (cache vs. run), CAS artifact digests, skill metadata—in a **single structured event** rather than scattered log lines. This \"wide event\" approach follows loggingsucks.com principles: one event per operation with all debugging context included.\n\nThe runservice observability system solves this by emitting **wide events** to NDJSON files whenever a skill executes, capturing the full operation lifecycle in a format that external tools (OTEL Collector, Prometheus) can consume.\n\n## Details\n\n### Event Emission Flow\n\nWhen `ExecuteSync` runs a skill [2a], it calls `emitWideEventWithArtifacts` to create an observability span. The system uses **`StartSpanAt`** [2b] to build a wide event with a specific start time, ensuring accurate duration measurements.\n\n### Correlation ID as Trace ID\n\nA key design decision: the **correlation ID becomes the trace ID** [2c]. This enables cross-layer correlation—the same trace ID links events from runservice, the skill binary, and any downstream operations. When a skill execution has a correlation ID, it's explicitly set via `WithSpanTraceID` to make it authoritative.\n\n### Context Enrichment\n\nThe event builder accumulates context through method chaining:\n- Component type (skill) and command name identify what ran\n- `WithSpanSubtype(\"runservice\")` distinguishes runservice-side events from skill-side events\n- Domain-specific data like `source` (run/cache), `cache_hit`, and `correlation_id` provide operational context\n\n### Artifact Digests for Replay\n\nThe system extracts **CAS digests from result envelopes** and adds them via `WithResultArtifact` [2d]. This enables **full response replay**—given just the observability event, you can retrieve the complete skill output from CAS storage.\n\n### Automatic Emission\n\nThe span pattern provides a **`done` callback** [2e] that automatically finalizes and emits the event based on the error status. If `err` is nil, it emits a success event; otherwise, it emits an error event with classified error type. This happens in `observability.Emit`, which applies tail sampling before writing to disk.\n\n### Tail Sampling\n\nNot all events are written—the sampler always records errors and slow requests (\u003e1s by default), but only samples 5% of healthy fast requests. This keeps disk usage manageable while ensuring debugging-critical events are never dropped."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "title": "Span Pattern with Automatic Emission",
      "description": "Observability infrastructure - shows the span pattern that provides automatic event emission via done callback with error handling",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "3a",
          "path": "internal/runtime/observability/span.go",
          "lineNumber": 148,
          "lineContent": "func StartSpan(ctx context.Context, op string, opts ...SpanOpt) (context.Context, func(error), *EventBuilder) {",
          "title": "Span Creation",
          "description": "Creates span with context, done callback, and builder for mid-flight enrichment"
        },
        {
          "id": "3b",
          "path": "internal/runtime/observability/span.go",
          "lineNumber": 167,
          "lineContent": "ctx, traceID := EnsureTraceID(ctx)",
          "title": "Trace ID Initialization",
          "description": "Ensures trace ID exists in context, generating new one if needed"
        },
        {
          "id": "3c",
          "path": "internal/runtime/observability/span.go",
          "lineNumber": 169,
          "lineContent": "b := NewEvent(op).WithTraceID(traceID)",
          "title": "Event Builder Setup",
          "description": "Creates event builder with operation type and trace ID"
        },
        {
          "id": "3d",
          "path": "internal/runtime/observability/span.go",
          "lineNumber": 198,
          "lineContent": "done := func(err error) {",
          "title": "Done Callback Definition",
          "description": "Defines callback that finalizes event based on error status and emits it"
        },
        {
          "id": "3e",
          "path": "internal/runtime/observability/span.go",
          "lineNumber": 202,
          "lineContent": "Emit(ctx, b.Success(dur))",
          "title": "Success Emission",
          "description": "Emits successful event when done callback receives nil error"
        },
        {
          "id": "3f",
          "path": "internal/runtime/observability/span.go",
          "lineNumber": 206,
          "lineContent": "Emit(ctx, b.Error(err, dur))",
          "title": "Error Emission",
          "description": "Emits error event when done callback receives non-nil error"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Span Pattern with Automatic Emission\n└── StartSpan() entry point \u003c-- 3a\n    ├── StartSpanAt() implementation \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:154\n    │   ├── EnsureTraceID(ctx) \u003c-- 3b\n    │   │   └── generates ULID if missing \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/context.go:64\n    │   ├── NewEvent(op).WithTraceID() \u003c-- 3c\n    │   │   └── creates EventBuilder\n    │   ├── apply span options \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:156\n    │   │   ├── WithParentID() \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:170\n    │   │   ├── WithComponent() \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:173\n    │   │   ├── WithCommand() \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:176\n    │   │   └── WithWorkspace() \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:185\n    │   ├── EnrichFromEnv/Context \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:196\n    │   └── done callback definition \u003c-- 3d\n    │       ├── if err == nil \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:201\n    │       │   └── Emit(Success) \u003c-- 3e\n    │       ├── if context.Canceled \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:203\n    │       │   └── Emit(Canceled) \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:204\n    │       └── else \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:205\n    │           └── Emit(Error) \u003c-- 3f\n    └── returns (ctx, done, builder) \u003c-- internal/runtime/observability/span.go:210",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen building distributed systems with multiple execution layers (CLI, runservice, job executor, skill processes), you need a way to **trace operations end-to-end** without manually threading trace IDs through every function call. The span pattern solves this by providing a **single function call** that:\n\n1. Ensures a trace ID exists in the context\n2. Creates an event builder pre-configured with operation metadata\n3. Returns a `done(error)` callback that **automatically emits** the right observability event (success/error/canceled) based on how the operation completes\n\nThis eliminates boilerplate and ensures **consistent observability** across all code paths, including error paths that developers often forget to instrument.\n\n## Details\n\n### The Pattern\n\n`StartSpan()` [3a] is the entry point that wraps `StartSpanAt()` [3a→154] with the current time. The function does three things in sequence:\n\n**1. Trace ID initialization** - `EnsureTraceID()` [3b] checks if a trace ID exists in the context, generating a new ULID [3b→64] if missing. This ensures every operation has a correlation ID for distributed tracing.\n\n**2. Event builder setup** - Creates a new `EventBuilder` [3c] with the operation type and trace ID, then applies optional configuration through `SpanOpt` functions [156]. Common options include `WithParentID()` [170] for nested spans, `WithComponent()` [173] to tag the layer (skill/cli/job), `WithCommand()` [176] for the skill name, and `WithWorkspace()` [185] for business context. The builder is then enriched [196] with session IDs and agent IDs from environment variables.\n\n**3. Done callback creation** - The `done` callback [3d] captures the start time and uses a switch statement to determine the final event status. If `err == nil` [201], it emits a success event [3e]. If the error is `context.Canceled` [203], it emits a canceled event [204]. Otherwise, it emits an error event [3f] with error classification. The duration is automatically calculated as `time.Since(startedAt)`.\n\n### Usage Pattern\n\nThe function returns three values [210]: the context (potentially with a new trace ID), the done callback, and the event builder. Callers typically use:\n\n```go\nctx, done, span := observability.StartSpan(ctx, observability.OpSkillRun, ...)\ndefer func() { done(err) }()\nspan.WithData(\"files\", count) // mid-flight enrichment\n```\n\nThe **deferred done callback** ensures the event is emitted even if the function panics or returns early. The returned builder allows **mid-flight enrichment** - adding domain-specific data as it becomes available during execution.\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThis pattern appears in both runservice [2b] and skillmain [5a], creating **dual-layer observability** where both the orchestration layer and the skill execution layer emit correlated events. The correlation works because runservice propagates its correlation_id as the trace_id [2c], which child processes inherit via `FOXCTL_TRACE_ID` environment variable [8c→8d]."
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "title": "Job Executor Observability with Background Enrichment",
      "description": "Job executor integration - demonstrates parallel enrichment pattern to avoid blocking on cloud metadata lookups during skill execution",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "4a",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 199,
          "lineContent": "ctx, traceID := observability.EnsureTraceID(ctx)",
          "title": "Trace ID Initialization",
          "description": "Ensures trace context exists before skill execution for propagation"
        },
        {
          "id": "4b",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 213,
          "lineContent": "go func() {",
          "title": "Background Enrichment",
          "description": "Starts goroutine to enrich event with environment context in parallel with execution"
        },
        {
          "id": "4c",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 228,
          "lineContent": "stdout, stderr, runErr := e.runSkill(ctx, opts.Manifest, opts.ArtifactPath, opts.Input)",
          "title": "Skill Execution",
          "description": "Executes skill while enrichment happens in background"
        },
        {
          "id": "4d",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 246,
          "lineContent": "observability.Emit(ctx, eventBuilder.Error(runErr, duration))",
          "title": "Error Event Emission",
          "description": "Emits error event if skill execution fails"
        },
        {
          "id": "4e",
          "path": "internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 277,
          "lineContent": "observability.Emit(ctx, eventBuilder.Success(duration))",
          "title": "Success Event Emission",
          "description": "Emits success event after validating envelope and writing result"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Job Executor Skill Execution Flow\n├── executeSkill() entry \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:189\n│   ├── EnsureTraceID(ctx) \u003c-- 4a\n│   ├── Background enrichment goroutine \u003c-- 4b\n│   │   └── EnrichFromEnv() + workspace \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:214\n│   ├── runSkill() execution \u003c-- 4c\n│   │   └── skillExecutor.Execute() \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:318\n│   ├── Error path \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:244\n│   │   ├── handleFailure() \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:247\n│   │   └── Emit error event \u003c-- 4d\n│   └── Success path \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:251\n│       ├── handleSuccess() \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:360\n│       │   ├── Unmarshal envelope \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:367\n│       │   ├── Validate envelope \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:376\n│       │   └── WriteFile result \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:386\n│       └── Emit success event \u003c-- 4e\n└── Parallel enrichment completion \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:235\n    └── Wait for enriched builder \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:241",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen the job executor runs a skill, it needs to emit **observability events** that capture what happened during execution - success or failure, duration, and context like workspace and job ID. The challenge is that enriching these events with environment context (session IDs, agent IDs) can be slow due to cloud metadata lookups that may timeout in non-cloud environments. The solution is to **enrich events in a background goroutine** while the skill executes, so observability never blocks the critical path [4b].\n\n## Details\n\n### Trace ID Initialization\n\nThe executor first ensures a **trace ID exists in the context** [4a] using `EnsureTraceID()`. This trace ID will be propagated to the skill process via environment variables, enabling correlation between executor-side and skill-side observability events.\n\n### Parallel Enrichment Pattern\n\nBefore executing the skill, the executor spawns a **background goroutine** [4b] that creates an enriched event builder by calling `EnrichFromEnv()` and looking up the workspace from the job directory. This enrichment happens **in parallel with skill execution** [4c], with a 2-second timeout to prevent indefinite blocking.\n\n### Execution and Event Emission\n\nThe executor calls `runSkill()` [4c], which delegates to `skillExecutor.Execute()`. After execution completes, the code waits for the enriched builder (or uses a baseline builder if enrichment times out).\n\nIf execution fails, the executor emits an **error event** [4d] with the error details and duration. If execution succeeds, it validates the result envelope and writes it to disk before emitting a **success event** [4e]. For skill-returned error envelopes (status=\"error\" in the envelope), the executor still emits an error event for observability purposes, even though the envelope was successfully produced.\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThis pattern ensures **observability never slows down skill execution**. Cloud metadata lookups that might take 500ms+ happen in parallel, and if they timeout, the skill still completes normally with a baseline event. The tail sampling system (always sample errors/slow requests) means critical debugging information is always captured without impacting performance."
    },
    {
